Loom AIE2P array plans: a streamed shared memory-tile panel may replay more than 63 times. The memory tile's lock
value field is 6 bits, and a streamed panel counts one lock unit per replay (the fill takes R credits and grants R
ready), so R = 64 (a 4096-token NPU call: 64 M blocks of 64 rows) did not encode. Past 63 replays (R even, R / 2 at
most 63) a member counts replay PAIRS: credits start at R / 2, the fill takes R / 2 and grants R / 2, each drain task
is two chained descriptors over the same slice (the first acquires one ready, its twin releases one credit), and the
streamed push queues R / 2 - 1 repeats. The owner and the members reserve the twins' descriptors. Panels of at most
63 replays emit byte-identical. EXPERIMENT LOOM_EXP_PAIR_MIN=n pair-counts every even count past n (a test of the pair
path at small counts: a 2048-token set built so runs bit-identical to the plain one).

